### Requests for the IntelliJ HTTP Client / VS Code REST Client.
### Start the stack first: docker compose up -d, then ./mvnw -pl agent-app spring-boot:test-run

@keycloak = http://localhost:8180
@agent = http://localhost:8080

### Token as operator (olena)
# @name tokenOlena
POST {{keycloak}}/realms/workflow/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=workflow-web&username=olena&password=olena

> {% client.global.set("olena_token", response.body.access_token); %}

### Token as approver (max)
# @name tokenMax
POST {{keycloak}}/realms/workflow/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=workflow-web&username=max&password=max

> {% client.global.set("max_token", response.body.access_token); %}

### agent-app health (public)
GET {{agent}}/actuator/health

### agent-app without a token -> 401
GET {{agent}}/api/v1/instances

### agent-app with a token -> 404 until M1 adds the instances API
GET {{agent}}/api/v1/instances
Authorization: Bearer {{olena_token}}

### mock-crm-mcp health
GET http://localhost:8091/actuator/health

### mock-rates health
GET http://localhost:8092/actuator/health

### Mailpit: latest messages (inbound requests and agent replies)
GET http://localhost:8025/api/v1/messages?limit=10
